{% extends "@core/base.p2" %}

{% comment %}
  Sign-in form.

  The form posts to itself and the password field is never repopulated. A
  framework that remembered a submitted password so the user could "try again"
  would write it into the browser's form state, and into whatever a misconfigured
  cache stored of the page.

  The failure message is one value for every reason the attempt failed, and it is
  the caller's job to pass that one value: the difference between "no such
  account" and "wrong password" is what an enumeration attack reads.
{% endcomment %}

{% block title %}Sign in · {{ siteTitle|default:"Application" }}{% endblock %}

{% comment %}
  No navbar and no footer: whoever reaches this page holds no identity, so the
  navbar could offer them only an empty brand and a Sign out of nothing, and
  the footer would put build information on the one page the public sees. They
  opt out by overriding the blocks with nothing, which the base now allows by
  putting those elements inside the blocks rather than around them.

  With the brand gone from the navbar, the site name goes above the box: the
  page is still the front door, and the browser tab is not the only place it
  should say whose door this is.
{% endcomment %}
{% block header %}{% endblock %}
{% block footer %}{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<p class="has-text-centered title is-3">{{ siteTitle|default:"Application" }}</p>
<div class="columns is-centered">
  <div class="column is-half-tablet is-one-third-desktop">
    <div class="box">
      <h1 class="title is-4">Sign in</h1>

      {% if loginError %}
      <div class="notification is-danger is-light" role="alert">{{ loginError }}</div>
      {% endif %}

      <form method="post" action="{{ action|default:'/login' }}">
        {{ csrfInput }}

        <div class="field">
          <label class="label" for="wa-username">Username</label>
          <div class="control">
            <input
              class="input"
              type="text"
              id="wa-username"
              name="username"
              value="{{ username|default:'' }}"
              autocomplete="username"
              autocapitalize="none"
              spellcheck="false"
              required>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="field">
          <label class="label" for="wa-password">Password</label>
          <div class="control">
            <input
              class="input"
              type="password"
              id="wa-password"
              name="password"
              autocomplete="current-password"
              required>
          </div>
        </div>

        {% if next %}<input type="hidden" name="next" value="{{ next }}">{% endif %}

        <div class="field">
          <div class="control">
            <button type="submit" class="button is-primary is-fullwidth">Sign in</button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </form>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
{% endblock %}
